# MakGuard AI — Cursor Rules

## Project Context
This is a 48-hour hackathon project called MakGuard AI.
It is a mobile-responsive web application for AI-powered scam detection in Malaysia.
Always refer to the /docs folder for full project specifications before generating code.

## Stack Rules — Never Deviate
- Framework: Next.js 14 with App Router only. Never suggest Pages Router.
- Language: TypeScript only. Never use plain JavaScript or `any` types.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS only. Never write custom CSS files or inline styles.
- Components: Use shadcn/ui primitives. Never build UI components from scratch if shadcn has one.
- AI: Google Gemini 2.5 Flash API only. Never suggest OpenAI, Anthropic, or other providers.
- Database: Supabase with the JavaScript client only. Never suggest Prisma, Drizzle, or raw SQL files.
- Deployment target: Vercel. Never suggest Docker, custom servers, or containerization.

## Architecture Rules
- All Supabase queries must live inside /app/api/ server-side route handlers only.
- All Gemini API calls must live inside /app/api/ server-side route handlers only.
- All VirusTotal API calls must live inside /app/api/ server-side route handlers only.
- Never call any third-party API or Supabase directly from a client component.
- Client components must only call our own internal /api/ routes via fetch().

## Code Style Rules
- camelCase for variables and functions.
- PascalCase for React components and TypeScript interfaces.
- snake_case for all Supabase column names.
- No `any` types. Define proper TypeScript interfaces for all API responses.
- No TODO comments or placeholder code. Every function must be complete and working.
- Keep components small and single-purpose. One component per file.
- All components that use hooks or browser APIs must have the 'use client' directive.

## File Structure
- /app — Next.js App Router pages and layouts
- /app/api — All server-side API route handlers
- /components/ui — shadcn/ui base components (do not modify these)
- /components — Custom MakGuard components
- /lib — Utility functions, Supabase client, type definitions
- /docs — Project documentation only, no code here

## MVP Priority Rules
- If a feature is not listed in /docs/PRD.md under IN SCOPE, do not build it.
- Always ask: is this the simplest implementation that works for a demo?
- Optimize for demo reliability and mobile visual polish above all else.
- Never suggest real-time websockets, complex state management libraries, or custom middleware.
- If there are two ways to solve a problem, always choose the one with fewer dependencies.